## Context

This ticket turns the measurement protocol into a finite acquisition universe.
It prevents a broad collection from becoming an untestable claim of exhaustive
JETP finance.

## First test

Create a census fixture with a paginated inventory, a revised file, a blocked
URL and an unnamed slot. It must require a disposition for each expected item,
retain the source/version/route, and fail if an unresolved item is reported as
zero or complete.

## Actions

For each country and lifecycle state, freeze named official inventories, issuer,
version/snapshot, coverage period, retrieval route, item identity, expected page
or file count, event semantics, retention rule and stop condition. Include the
0815 common-source, operational-timing and comparator routes only where they
improve source interpretation; do not treat them as identification tests.
Specify raw-byte/DVC handling, review queue, controlled vocabulary and country
ticket workloads.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Country/source/period census is finite, versioned and reviewable
- [ ] Every expected item can receive admitted, duplicate, excluded, unavailable or lost-visibility disposition
- [ ] Each source documents financial-state and date semantics, not just a title or country label
- [ ] Candidate extraction, raw-byte retention and reviewed canonical admission remain distinct
- [ ] Four independent country ingestion handoffs are ready without overlapping authority

